From 20a9e0de31fab2650ee6702e16afe2be9bca20ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hergert <christian@sourceandstack.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:28:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/virtio: Recalculate ignore_damage_clips on every update

[ Upstream commit a9cc9905ddb7e7ce98e19b7e508aa3c78661afef, without the
  bo->dumb condition that 730f8554f35c ("drm/virtio: preserve damage
  clips for rendered resources") added before it ]

Plane state duplication preserves ignore_damage_clips. Once a commit
that changes the framebuffer sets it, every later update of the same
framebuffer (DIRTYFB) ignores its damage and transfers and flushes the
whole plane, because the flag is never cleared.

Assign ignore_damage_clips on every atomic check.

Reviewed-by: Lyude Paul <lyude@redhat.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260903211914.1109100-3-lyude@redhat.com
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
index 640815af409..cdd54829cf8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
@@ -116,8 +116,8 @@ static int virtio_gpu_plane_atomic_check(struct drm_plane *plane,
 	 * has changed since the last plane update (page-flip). In this case, a
 	 * full plane update should happen because uploads are done per-buffer.
 	 */
-	if (old_plane_state->fb != new_plane_state->fb)
-		new_plane_state->ignore_damage_clips = true;
+	new_plane_state->ignore_damage_clips =
+		old_plane_state->fb != new_plane_state->fb;
 
 	crtc_state = drm_atomic_get_crtc_state(state,
 					       new_plane_state->crtc);
-- 
